  <data name="Cli.Help" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>APFS for Windows: opens Mac APFS disks read-only on Windows.

Usage:
  apfs info &lt;source&gt;                         Shows container and volume information
  apfs ls &lt;source&gt; [path] [-r] [--hash]      Lists the contents of a folder
  apfs extract &lt;source&gt; &lt;path&gt; &lt;target&gt;      Copies a file to Windows
  apfs check &lt;source&gt; [--full]               Read-only self-check (reads all files, compares counters and name hashes);
                                             --full: structural consistency (block ownership, space manager, reference counts)
  apfs dump &lt;source&gt;                         Dumps internal structures (development: checkpoint, space manager, volume superblocks)
  apfs mount &lt;source&gt; [X:]                   Mounts volumes as drive letters (Ctrl+C unmounts);
                                             if there are several volumes each gets its own letter; --all for internal volumes
  apfs register / unregister                 (Administrator) WinFsp registration for physical disks

&lt;source&gt;: disk image file or \\.\PhysicalDriveN (requires administrator rights)
Options: --volume N (volume index, default 0), --partition N (APFS partition index)
Encrypted volumes: --password-prompt (asks for the password) or --password-stdin (reads the password from standard input)</value>
  </data>
